mes normal and the system drifts back to a ball of mud; code review alone depends on memory and discipline and does not scale. Move enforcement from people to CI."}, {"id": "src_content_module_13_06_modular_monolith_advanced_when_modular_monolith", "label": "When to Prefer Modular Monolith over Microservices", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/content/module-13/06-modular-monolith-advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Choose it when the team is small, domain boundaries are unsettled, and no platform/infra team exists: defer distributed-system costs while keeping boundary discipline."}, {"id": "src_content_module_13_06_modular_monolith_advanced_adr_modular_monolith_orders", "label": "ADR: Modular Monolith for Order Management", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/content/module-13/06-modular-monolith-advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "6 engineers, unstable domain, no infra team: one deployable split by bounded context with build rules blocking cross-internal imports; easy to extract a service later."}], "edges": [{"source": "src_content_module_13_06_modular_monolith_advanced_modular_monolith", "target": "src_content_module_13_06_modular_monolith_advanced_ball_of_mud", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/content/module-13/06-modular-monolith-advanced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_content_module_13_06_modular_monolith_advanced_modular_monolith", "target": "src_content_module_13_06_modular_monolith_advanced_boundary_enforcement", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/content/module-13/06-modular-monolith-advanced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_content_module_13_06_modu